<Window x:Class="Bws.Gui.CatalogueWindow"
        xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        Title="{Binding Heading}"
        Background="{DynamicResource ApplicationBackgroundBrush}"
        UseLayoutRounding="True"
        SnapsToDevicePixels="True"
        TextOptions.TextFormattingMode="Display"
        TextOptions.TextRenderingMode="ClearType"
        Height="900" Width="1400"
        MinHeight="{StaticResource HeightWindowLeast}" MinWidth="{StaticResource WidthWindowLeast}"
        FocusManager.FocusedElement="{Binding ElementName=SheetScroll}">

    <!--
        EVERY COMPONENT THIS WINDOW IS BUILT OUT OF, ON ONE SHEET. Rule 4 of the owner's GUI rules
        asks for this screen, and 2026-09-10 is the day it did not exist - checked before building
        it rather than assumed.

        REACHED ONLY BY A LAUNCH ARGUMENT, and it ships in every configuration. Compiling it out
        of Release would mean the sheet could only ever be photographed from a Debug build, and
        this project has already paid for that exact confusion once: screens.ps1 photographed
        Debug while somebody had just built Release, and the pictures were correct pictures of a
        different file.

        THE MARKUP HERE IS A HEADER AND A LIST. Everything about how a component is drawn lives in
        Themes/Catalogue.xaml, which is where the rest of this window's look lives too - so a
        person changing how the sheet reads changes one file, and it is not this one.

        THE FOUR ATTRIBUTES ABOVE ARE COPIED FROM MainWindow.xaml ON PURPOSE. Layout rounding,
        pixel snapping and the two text options decide whether text is drawn with ClearType, and a
        catalogue rendering its samples differently from the window that ships would be a
        catalogue of something else. docs/10 records what turning one of them off cost: 80,5 per
        cent of text pixels picked up colour fringing.
    -->

    <Grid Grid.IsSharedSizeScope="True">

        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            <RowDefinition Height="*" />
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <!--
            WHAT THE SHEET SAYS ABOUT ITSELF, and the middle line is the one that matters: how
            many components are declared against how many are drawn here. Rule 4 says a catalogue
            may not leave anything out, and a count printed beside the sheet is how a person
            checks that without counting rows.
        -->
        <Border Grid.Row="0"
                Background="{DynamicResource SurfacePanel}"
                BorderBrush="{DynamicResource SurfacePanelEdge}"
                BorderThickness="{StaticResource BorderFooterRule}"
                Padding="{StaticResource PaddingPanel}">

            <StackPanel>
                <TextBlock Text="{Binding Heading}" Style="{StaticResource HeadingText}" />

                <TextBlock x:Name="CountedText"
                           Text="{Binding Counted}"
                           Style="{StaticResource SubduedText}"
                           Margin="{StaticResource MarginAboveStatus}" />

                <TextBlock x:Name="NoteText"
                           Text="{Binding Note}"
                           Style="{StaticResource SubduedText}"
                           TextWrapping="Wrap" />
            </StackPanel>

        </Border>

        <!--
            FOCUSABLE, AND IT IS THE SCROLL VIEWER RATHER THAN ANYTHING IN IT. Measured 2026-09-10:
            without this, Page Down on a freshly opened catalogue does NOTHING - the sheet is fifty
            five rows long, nothing in it takes the keyboard by default, and a scroll viewer only
            answers keys when it has focus. The window hands it the focus below, so the first key
            press somebody makes on a long sheet does what they meant.
        -->
        <ScrollViewer Grid.Row="1"
                      x:Name="SheetScroll"
                      Focusable="True"
                      VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"
                      HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                      Padding="{StaticResource PaddingPanel}">

            <ItemsControl x:Name="Sheet"
                          ItemsSource="{Binding Groups}"
                          ItemTemplate="{StaticResource CatalogueGroup}"
                          Focusable="False" />

        </ScrollViewer>

    </Grid>

</Window>
